Description: Bayesian implementation of a joint multiscale species distribution
    model integrating global and regional information through cross-scale
    coupling in INLA via 'inlabru'. Requires 'nsdm.vinput' objects, as
    produced by the 'sabinaNSDM' package, and fits joint spatial Bayesian
    models with a broad-scale spatial field shared across scales plus a
    regional-only field for fine-scale residual autocorrelation. Supports
    presence-absence/background (binomial) and continuous presence-only
    (log-Gaussian Cox process) likelihoods. Provides multiple coupling
    architectures (unpooled, ordered-hierarchical, nested-shrinkage,
    scale-decomposed, Bayesian feedback) for the intercept and covariate terms
    independently, letting the regional model borrow strength from global
    patterns while accounting for scale-dependent niche shifts.
